#: aguard-safe.php:500
msgid ""
"AGuard Safe keeps a security log on this site and, if you have turned on its"
" optional checks, contacts the service of its author. The text below "
"describes exactly what the plugin does with the settings this site has now."
msgstr ""

#: aguard-safe.php:501
msgid "Suggested text:"
msgstr ""

#: aguard-safe.php:502
msgid ""
"This site uses the AGuard Safe security plugin to notice break-ins. The "
"plugin keeps a log of sign-ins, failed sign-in attempts and administrative "
"actions, together with the IP address and the browser name of whoever made "
"them. It also notes requests that look like a search for a weak spot (for "
"example, for a backup of the configuration file), with the IP address and "
"the browser name. The records are stored on this site, sign-ins and actions "
"for 90 days and such requests for 30 days, and are not shared with anyone."
msgstr ""

#: aguard-safe.php:504
msgid ""
"The plugin also uses a service run by its author, AGuard (data.aguard.lt):"
msgstr ""

#: aguard-safe.php:505
msgid ""
"once a day it sends the folder names and versions of the installed plugins "
"to learn about known vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""

#: aguard-safe.php:506
msgid ""
"When an administrator signs in, it sends the first 5 characters of a hash of"
" the password to check it against lists of leaked passwords; the password "
"itself is never sent."
msgstr ""

